{
 "_doc": "The audit loop's registry. gate.py reads it to decide who is due; each pass follows passes/<id>.md. Fields: watch/exclude are git globs (relative to the repo root); branches (optional) are globs of origin branches also watched while ahead of master; none are watched today, since class work lands on master through PRs and the old class branches still count hundreds of commits ahead after their merges; external lists outside sources ('wago_build': gate.py checks wago.tools for a newer 1.60 client build); external_every_h forces a pass that often for sources git can't see; max_quiet_days is a safety net; model is the subagent model for the pass ('sonnet' for mechanical passes, 'opus' where the pass judges mechanics or balance); sims marks passes that sim the report's requests on the new master (the loop runs them once and shares the run). branch_active_days: a branch ahead of master counts only while its newest commit is at most this many days old, so old unmerged branches don't trigger passes. owns: repo docs the pass keeps current besides its own audit files (committed with the run). wago_probe: how many build numbers past the newest one wago.tools lists the gate probes in the db2 exports (the builds list lags). skip_if_no_movement: after the loop's shared sims, the pass is skipped (recorded as quiet) when no report build moved more than 0.5 DPS against the previous shared run (ref/shared/summary.tsv), unless a changed file matches always_pass or the auditor is due for another reason. Leveling-only paths (**/*leveling*, **/leveling/**, the level 30 APLs) are excluded from the level 60 DPS auditors, as the old auditors excluded leveling-only work. healbench / tankbench: the pass runs tools/healbench or tools/tankbench itself (the healers aren't in the report's shared sims), so run healbench and tankbench passes one at a time like the sim passes. enabled: false keeps an auditor out of the gate.",
 "branch_active_days": 2,
 "wago_probe": 300,
